## Why This Is Asked
Tests the candidate's ability to enforce data residency, design cross-region reads for hot tenants, and plan DR while maintaining performance.

## Key Concepts
- Data residency policies and region tagging
- Per-tenant schema isolation and access controls
- Cross-region analytics cloning and cost/performance trade-offs
- DR testing and regulatory auditing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: routing by tenant region
switch (tenant.region) {
  case 'us-east-1': routeTo(usEastClient); break;
  case 'eu-west-1': routeTo(euWestClient); break;
  default: routeTo(analyticsClone);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce tenant relocation across regions without downtime?
- How would you audit data-access for regulatory purposes?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model regulatory data residency in a managed RDBMS with cross-region replication, plus practical routing, isolation, backup and DR testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Data residency routing and tenant isolation
- Aurora Global Database writer/read topology
- Per-tenant schemas vs. separate databases
- IAM, KMS, backups, DR drills, latency validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-router: selects region, endpoints, and access controls per-tenant
function routeRequest(tenantId, operation) {
  const region = residencyMap[tenantId];
  const writer = regionWriterEndpoint[region];
  const readers = regionReadEndpoints[region];
  return { writer, readers, region };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle a tenant migration from one residency region to another?
- What monitoring would you implement to detect cross-region lag impacting reads?

Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a cross-region, PCI-compliant streaming path with masking and robust DR. It probes data masking strategy, replication choice, and operational readiness.

Key Concepts
- Data masking in streaming CDC
- Cross-region replication and latency targets
- Encryption: TLS in transit, KMS at rest
- PITR window and RPO/RTO goals
- DR testing cadence and monitoring

Code Example
```javascript
// Simple masking example used in testing
function maskPII(value, field){
  if(!value) return null;
  switch(field){
    case 'ssn': return 'XXX-XX-' + value.slice(-4);
    case 'email': return '***@example.com';
    default: return 'REDACTED';
  }
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate masking at scale across schema changes?
- What metrics and alarms would you configure for DR drills and replication lag?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-region, multi-master transactional paths with real-time analytics, while honoring security and compliance constraints.

## Key Concepts
- DynamoDB Global Tables for low-latency multi-region writes
- CDC pipeline (Streams → Lambda → DMS/Debezium) to Aurora
- Conflict resolution and data governance for cross-region writes
- PCI-DSS residency and EU-centric encryption/backups

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lambda sample: process DynamoDB stream and push to Aurora via CDC
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  for (const rec of event.Records) {
    if (rec.eventName === 'INSERT' || rec.eventName === 'MODIFY') {
      const item = AWS.DynamoDB.Converter.unmarshall(rec.dynamodb.NewImage);
      await upsertAurora(item);
    }
  }
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle a write-conflict when two regions update the same item simultaneously?
- What monitoring and alerting would you implement to guarantee RPO and RTO targets under failover conditions?
